DTSTAMP:20260630T041950Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260705T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260705T180000
SUMMARY:Bushkill Watershed Weird Hike
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us for this point to point hike that will feature favorite old trails
  and some new connections between Easton and Wind Gap PA!\nThis time\, we 
 will meet at the Simon Silk Mill\, just off of Bushkill Drive\, and shuttl
 e with as few cars as possible up to Wind Gap.\nFrom here\, we will walk a
  brief section of road for a tenth of a mile to a rather new trail connect
 ion.\nWe'll continue through part of the wooded section of Ballas Park to 
 the former Nazareth Branch of the Lehigh and New England Railroad\, which 
 we'll follow south.\nWe'll reach Jacobsburg Environmental Education Center
  and continue through on the rail grade\, then take side trails that will 
 lead though more uplands as well as along the Bushkill Creek. We'll pass t
 hrough Henry's Woods\, and then make our way to the south part of the park
 .\nHere\, we'll pick up a new trail connection somewhat recently opened to
  Belfast.\nDepending on the status of new trail connections\, we'll either
  follow that\, or we'll continue south on another short road walk to Belfa
 st Junction. Here'll we will pick up the rail trail south into Stockertown
 .\nThere is a missing bit through Stockertown\, but it is being connected.
  Some of it is complete\, some is not.\nRegardless\, we have a route that 
 will be a bit different heading southbound anyway\, which will take us pas
 t an historic church\, along some back streets\, on some paved development
  trails\, and then down through meadows of Rappolt Field.\nWe'll turn from
  here along one more brief road walk to reach the former Easton and Northe
 rn rail line\, and this will take us almost all the way back to Simon Silk
  Mill to finish the hike. Distance will be about 15 miles.\nThere are a co
 uple of bar and grill places in Stockertown that we might make our lunch s
 top.\nIf needed\, contact me at 908 343 8374
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/metrotrails/events/315468534/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260629T131948Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260629T131948Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
