X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Montclairlocal": "https://montclairlocal.news/event/opera-mozarts-il-don-giovanni-da-pontes-1826-edition/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:montclairlocal
X-SOURCE:Montclair Local News
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260711T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260711T180000
DTSTAMP:20260628T190513Z
CREATED:20260628T190513Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260628T190513Z
UID:10140438-1783782000-1783792800@montclairlocal.news
SUMMARY:Opera--Mozart's Il Don Giovanni (Da Ponte's 1826 edition)
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate 200 years of Italian Opera in America — Mozart’s “Don Giovanni” was the first opera ever to become a permanent part of the international repertory\, from its premiere in 1787 to the present day. It was also the earliest work included in North America’s first season of Italian opera two hundred years ago–a production personally supervised and edited by Lorenzo da Ponte\, the original author of the text. Teatro Nuovo is restoring the form of the title he and Mozart used\, Il Don Giovanni\, and is taking the anniversary occasion to restore as well everything we can learn about the performance style of the work’s early life. It presents the famous drama in a streamlined\, brilliantly vivacious guise. Ricardo José Rivera\, the baritone star of Teatro Nuovo’s last three seasons and more recently of the Metropolitan Opera’s I Puritani\, returns in his first-ever portrayal of the Don; Geoffrey Loff leads the company’s celebrated original-instrument orchestra. The projected English titles come to us from Da Ponte’s son Luigi\, created for the printed 1826 libretto. Expect the unexpected! \nTeatro Nuovo presents Bel Canto classics and rarities with a period-instrument orchestra and a performing style the Wall Street Journal calls “transformative.” For more details\, visit TeatroNuovo.org \nPre-opera Serenade at 1:30pm: The Great Garcías (I). Music by three members of the amazing family that brought Bel Canto opera to the New World: Manuel García and his daughters Maria Malibran and Pauline Viardot. Presented by Teatro Nuovo’s Resident Artist Program (Timothy Cheung\, Director). \nPre-opera Lecture at 2:00pm: Will Crutchfield introduces “Il Don Giovanni” \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/opera-mozarts-il-don-giovanni-da-pontes-1826-edition/
LOCATION:Alexander Kasser Theater\, Montclair State University\, Montclair\, NJ\, 07042\, United States
CATEGORIES:Art & Culture
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://montclairlocal.news/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Teatro-Nuovo-Il-Don-Giovanni-with-logo-1920x1080_300.jpg
GEO:40.8615199;-74.1985521
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Alexander Kasser Theater Montclair State University Montclair NJ 07042 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=Montclair State University:geo:-74.1985521,40.8615199
END:VEVENT
