X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Libcal Bccls 10306": "https://bccls.libcal.com/calendar/montclair/toritos"}
X-SOURCE-ID:libcal_bccls_10306
X-SOURCE:Libcal Bccls 10306
DTSTART:20260711T190000Z
DTEND:20260711T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260711T000000Z
SUMMARY:Los Toritos de Pucará: Peruvuan Craft Painting Workshop (Children ages 5  and Adults)
DESCRIPTION:The Consulate General of Peru in Paterson offers a Torito de 
 Pucará painting workshop for both adults and children. Through this 
 activity\, participants learn about the cultural significance of the Torito 
 de Pucará while enjoying a relaxed and creative painting experience. 
 Participants will take home their own painted Torito at the end of the 
 workshop. Registration recommended.\n\n \n\nAbout the Toritos de 
 Pucará\n\nThe Toritos de Pucará are an iconic Peruvian craft originating 
 from the town of Pucará\, in the Puno region. These ceramic figures\, 
 which depict bulls adorned with vibrant colors and intricate patterns\, 
 have roots that trace back to pre-Hispanic times\, influenced by the 
 Pucará culture\, which flourished between 500 B.C. and 200 A.D. in 
 Peru’s highland region. The significance of the Toritos de Pucará is 
 deeply connected to protection\, prosperity\, and fertility. 
 Traditionally\, they are placed on the rooftops of homes as amulets to 
 attract good luck\, abundant harvests\, and protection for the family and 
 household. The bull\, a strong and resilient animal\, is seen as a guardian 
 that wards off negative energies and draws in abundance. Over time\, and 
 following the arrival of the Spanish\, the Toritos de Pucará were 
 incorporated into Christian beliefs\, where the figure of the bull came to 
 symbolize sacrifice and spiritual strength. In this way\, these figures 
 became a cultural icon of the Andean region\, representing a syncretism 
 between ancient agricultural traditions and new religious influences.\n 
 \n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Children's Floor\, Montclair Main - Green Room
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Children's Programs
UID:LibCal-10306-16047835
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/calendar/montclair/toritos
END:VEVENT
