SUMMARY:Create Your Own Indian Paper Quill Earrings NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nPaper quilling arrived in India as a modernized handicraft in 
 the late 20th centuries. Indian artisans quickly embraced the medium\, 
 pairing the technique with the country's rich history of paper-making and 
 making it their own. In this class traditional artist and artisan Ajita 
 Shah teaches you how to create a variety of beautiful and unusual earrings 
 out of paper quills.\n\nCo-sponsored by the Folklife Center of Northern New 
 Jersey. This program goes along with the Paved With Promise suitcase 
 exhibition commemorating the 1965 Immigration and Nationality Act which 
 opened up the United States to groups in Asia\, South America and other 
 areas that had been previously restricted.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Classroom\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Arts & Crafts
UID:LibCal-10306-16945514
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16945514
END:VEVENT
