SUMMARY:Let's Talk About Formula One NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nFormula 1 represents the pinnacle of auto racing. It emerged 
 from the tradition of the Grand Prix in the early 20th century but the 
 sport as we know it started after World War II\, with open-wheeled cars\, 
 teams\, drivers and sponsors of the highest caliber competing on 
 road-courses around the globe. Today Formula 1 is experiencing 
 unprecedented global growth\, shifting from a niche motorsport into a mass 
 entertainment juggernaut. \n\nWe’ll talk about the history and evolution 
 of the sport and how the present-day players have transformed it and 
 continue to shape it. Where do you hope to see Formula 1 in 20 years? Will 
 the classic race-courses survive? Will the diversity of design\, 
 race-courses and drivers flourish? Or will it just become another packaged 
 entertainment spectacle? Come prepared to share your own ideas! \n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Classroom\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School
UID:LibCal-10306-16747973
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16747973
END:VEVENT
