SUMMARY:Pollinator Meadow Volunteer Workday
DESCRIPTION:South Mountain Conservancy Activities Meetup Group\nPollinator
  Meadow activities will focus on pathway installation and invasive species
  sweep and removal. Work is strenuous to moderate. Ages 12 to 15 are welco
 me with a parent or guardian present. Ages 15 and above require a signatur
 e by a parent or guardian on a [liability waiver](https://1drv.ms/b/c/d5fb
 9d3835660a78/IQCJO4IIj6GnQ6N4RuNC981xAYL2kFajs9_RL8f8V7NkhaM?e=5bd5oi)\; t
 eenagers cannot just be dropped off.\n\nPlease arrive 5 to 10 minutes earl
 y so we can start promptly at 10 am.\n\nPlease dress appropriately! Wear l
 ong pants\, long-sleeved shirt\, closed-toe shoes or rain boots. please no
  bug spray. Wear sunscreen and a hat. We supply tools. If you have gloves\
 , bring them or you can borrow a pair from us. Bring your own water.\n\nYo
 u can download a copy of our [liability waiver](https://1drv.ms/b/c/d5fb9d
 3835660a78/IQCJO4IIj6GnQ6N4RuNC981xAYL2kFajs9_RL8f8V7NkhaM?e=5bd5oi) to pr
 int\, sign and bring to the event.\n\nWe occasionally use photos of events
  in promotional materials and social media. By attending the event\, I con
 sent to photos of me being used in promotional materials or on social medi
 a.\n\nFor information\, contact program coordinator Lori LaBorde at citize
 nscience@[somocon.org](http://somocon.org/)\n\n**Meet at the meadow after 
 parking in Shady Nook Picnic Area.**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/somocon/events/315393175/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260624T035229Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260624T035229Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
